-- Diplomatic Appointments (Selection Process) Bill 2026 (Cth), first reading print (Senate),
-- 7 September 2026 (file 26S2721).
-- Cases: #ASSERTs exercising every encoded provision, its boundaries, and both readings of every
-- fork in registers/fork-register.json on the facts that divide them.
-- All people, offices' holders and dates here are invented for the tests.

IMPORT `part4-miscellaneous`

§ `Builders for the tests`

GIVEN n  IS A STRING
      ms IS A LIST OF Membership
      es IS A LIST OF `MOP(S) Act engagement`
      ss IS A LIST OF `State or Territory staff engagement`
      rs IS A LIST OF `party role`
      aps IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Person
`a person named` n `with memberships` ms `, MOP(S) Act engagements` es `, State or Territory engagements` ss `, party roles` rs `and APS employment` aps MEANS
    Person WITH
        `name`                                 IS n
        `memberships`                          IS ms
        `MOP(S) Act engagements`               IS es
        `State or Territory staff engagements` IS ss
        `party roles`                          IS rs
        `is an APS employee`                   IS aps

GIVEN c IS A Person
GIVETH A `list entry`
`listed with reasons` c MEANS
    `list entry` WITH `candidate` IS c, `the list sets out reasons despite the affiliation` IS TRUE

GIVEN c IS A Person
GIVETH A `list entry`
`listed without reasons` c MEANS
    `list entry` WITH `candidate` IS c, `the list sets out reasons despite the affiliation` IS FALSE

-- A Committee whose instruments, membership and meeting are in order; what varies is given.
GIVEN e       IS A NUMBER
      l       IS A NUMBER
      es      IS A LIST OF `list entry`
      present IS A NUMBER
      vf      IS A NUMBER
      va      IS A NUMBER
      nd      IS A NUMBER
      nc      IS A `notice content`
GIVETH A `Selection Committee`
`a Committee established on` e `, given on` l `the list` es `, meeting with` present `present voting` vf `to` va `, giving on` nd `notice` nc MEANS
    `Selection Committee` WITH
        `established on`                                   IS e
        `established by written instrument`                IS TRUE
        `members appointed`                                IS 3
        `members appointed by written instrument`          IS TRUE
        `the members have an appropriate balance under s 12(5)` IS TRUE
        `list given`                                       IS TRUE
        `list given on`                                    IS l
        `list`                                             IS es
        `decision made at a meeting`                       IS TRUE
        `members present at the meeting`                   IS present
        `votes for`                                        IS vf
        `votes against`                                    IS va
        `notice given`                                     IS TRUE
        `notice given on`                                  IS nd
        `notice`                                           IS nc

-- A Committee established and given its list that has not yet decided.
GIVEN e  IS A NUMBER
      l  IS A NUMBER
      es IS A LIST OF `list entry`
GIVETH A `Selection Committee`
`an undecided Committee established on` e `, list given on` l `with the list` es MEANS
    `Selection Committee` WITH
        `established on`                                   IS e
        `established by written instrument`                IS TRUE
        `members appointed`                                IS 3
        `members appointed by written instrument`          IS TRUE
        `the members have an appropriate balance under s 12(5)` IS TRUE
        `list given`                                       IS TRUE
        `list given on`                                    IS l
        `list`                                             IS es
        `decision made at a meeting`                       IS FALSE
        `members present at the meeting`                   IS 0
        `votes for`                                        IS 0
        `votes against`                                    IS 0
        `notice given`                                     IS FALSE
        `notice given on`                                  IS 0
        `notice`                                           IS `referring the matter back to the Minister`

-- An appointment by the Governor-General, no s 9(3) satisfaction, no resolutions, no tabling;
-- the Minister knows the facts; not terminated.
GIVEN p    IS A Person
      o    IS AN Office
      made IS A NUMBER
      term IS A NUMBER
      prev IS A NUMBER
      cs   IS A LIST OF `Selection Committee`
GIVETH AN Appointment
`the appointment of` p `to` o `made on` made `, term from` term `, after an appointment on` prev `, with Committees` cs MEANS
    Appointment WITH
        `office`                                              IS o
        `appointee`                                           IS p
        `made on`                                             IS made
        `term starts on`                                      IS term
        `made by the Governor-General`                        IS TRUE
        `the previous appointment to the office was made on`  IS prev
        `Selection Committees for the office`                 IS cs
        `the Minister is satisfied the appointee has no significant political affiliation` IS FALSE
        `the Senate passed a resolution approving it`         IS FALSE
        `the Senate's resolution was passed on`               IS 0
        `the House passed a resolution approving it`          IS FALSE
        `the House's resolution was passed on`                IS 0
        `a statement of reasons was tabled in the Senate`     IS FALSE
        `the Senate statement was tabled on`                  IS 0
        `a statement of reasons was tabled in the House`      IS FALSE
        `the House statement was tabled on`                   IS 0
        `the Minister is aware of the facts of any failure to comply` IS TRUE
        `terminated as soon as practicable after the Minister became aware` IS FALSE

-- The same, made under s 9(3): the Minister's satisfaction and each House's resolution given.
GIVEN p    IS A Person
      o    IS AN Office
      made IS A NUMBER
      prev IS A NUMBER
      cs   IS A LIST OF `Selection Committee`
      sat  IS A BOOLEAN
      sres IS A BOOLEAN
      son  IS A NUMBER
      hres IS A BOOLEAN
      hon  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN Appointment
`the s 9(3) appointment of` p `to` o `made on` made `, after an appointment on` prev `, with Committees` cs `, Minister satisfied` sat `, Senate resolving` sres `on` son `, House resolving` hres `on` hon MEANS
    Appointment WITH
        `office`                                              IS o
        `appointee`                                           IS p
        `made on`                                             IS made
        `term starts on`                                      IS made PLUS 14
        `made by the Governor-General`                        IS TRUE
        `the previous appointment to the office was made on`  IS prev
        `Selection Committees for the office`                 IS cs
        `the Minister is satisfied the appointee has no significant political affiliation` IS sat
        `the Senate passed a resolution approving it`         IS sres
        `the Senate's resolution was passed on`               IS son
        `the House passed a resolution approving it`          IS hres
        `the House's resolution was passed on`                IS hon
        `a statement of reasons was tabled in the Senate`     IS FALSE
        `the Senate statement was tabled on`                  IS 0
        `a statement of reasons was tabled in the House`      IS FALSE
        `the House statement was tabled on`                   IS 0
        `the Minister is aware of the facts of any failure to comply` IS TRUE
        `terminated as soon as practicable after the Minister became aware` IS FALSE

GIVEN p    IS A Person
      o    IS AN Office
      made IS A NUMBER
      occ  IS AN Occasion
GIVETH AN `acting arrangement`
`an arrangement for` p `to act as` o `made on` made `during` occ MEANS
    `acting arrangement` WITH
        `office`                IS o
        `the chargé d’affaires` IS p
        `made on`               IS made
        `occasion`              IS occ
        `the Minister is aware of the facts of any failure to comply` IS TRUE
        `terminated as soon as practicable after the Minister became aware` IS FALSE

§ `The world`

-- Royal Assent on Monday 1 March 2027, so the Act commences on Tuesday 2 March 2027.
-- Holidays: Anzac Day, Tuesday 25 April 2028. Sitting days in September 2028 as below; the Senate
-- sits on Friday 1 September, the day of one appointment.
`the world` MEANS World WITH
    `the day of the Royal Assent`           IS `the day` 2027 3 1
    `holidays`                              IS LIST `the day` 2028 4 25
    `Senate sitting days`                   IS LIST `the day` 2028 9 1, `the day` 2028 9 4, `the day` 2028 9 5, `the day` 2028 9 6, `the day` 2028 9 7, `the day` 2028 9 11, `the day` 2028 9 12
    `House of Representatives sitting days` IS LIST `the day` 2028 9 5, `the day` 2028 9 6, `the day` 2028 9 7, `the day` 2028 9 12, `the day` 2028 9 13, `the day` 2028 9 14

-- A world in which the Act commences on 29 February 2028 (Royal Assent on 28 February).
`the leap world` MEANS World WITH
    `the day of the Royal Assent`           IS `the day` 2028 2 28
    `holidays`                              IS EMPTY
    `Senate sitting days`                   IS EMPTY
    `House of Representatives sitting days` IS EMPTY

§ `Acts Interpretation Act boundary (aia-time.l4)`

#ASSERT `the day` 1970 1 1 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the day` 2026 10 2 EQUALS 20728
#ASSERT (`the civil date of` (`the day` 2028 2 29))'s `day of month` EQUALS 29
#ASSERT (`the civil date of` (`the day` 2028 2 29))'s `month` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the weekday of` (`the day` 2026 10 2) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `is a Saturday or a Sunday` (`the day` 2018 3 31)

-- s 2G(2), Example 1: 6 months starting on 15 December end immediately before 15 June.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 6 `months starting on` (`the day` 2027 12 15) EQUALS `the day` 2028 6 14
-- s 2G(2), Example 2: 6 months starting on 31 October end at the end of April.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 6 `months starting on` (`the day` 2027 10 31) EQUALS `the day` 2028 4 30
-- s 2G(1), Example 2: a month starting on 31 August ends at the end of September.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 `months starting on` (`the day` 2027 8 31) EQUALS `the day` 2027 9 30

-- s 36(2), its example: a last day of Saturday 31 March moves to Monday 2 April.
#ASSERT `the last day for doing a thing, given s 36(2), when the stated last day is` (`the day` 2018 3 31) `and the holidays are` EMPTY EQUALS `the day` 2018 4 2
-- A holiday: Tuesday 25 April 2028 moves to Wednesday 26 April.
#ASSERT `the last day for doing a thing, given s 36(2), when the stated last day is` (`the day` 2028 4 25) `and the holidays are` (LIST `the day` 2028 4 25) EQUALS `the day` 2028 4 26
-- A weekday that is no holiday stays put.
#ASSERT `the last day for doing a thing, given s 36(2), when the stated last day is` (`the day` 2028 4 24) `and the holidays are` (LIST `the day` 2028 4 25) EQUALS `the day` 2028 4 24

-- s 2M: sitting days of the Senate after 1 September up to 11 September 2028: five.
#ASSERT `the number of sitting days after` (`the day` 2028 9 1) `up to and including` (`the day` 2028 9 11) `among` (`the world`'s `Senate sitting days`) EQUALS 5

-- s 3A(2) is displaced by s 2 (s 3A(1)); kept for the boundary only.
#ASSERT `the default commencement day for an Act assented to on` (`the day` 2027 3 1) EQUALS `the day` 2027 3 29

