§ `Part 1 -- s 8: the tests`

-- s 8(1)
#ASSERT `has a disqualifying political affiliation on` `Drew` `the test day`
#ASSERT `has a disqualifying political affiliation on` `Casey` `the test day`
#ASSERT NOT `has a disqualifying political affiliation on` `Ellis` `the test day`
#ASSERT NOT `has a disqualifying political affiliation on` `Alex` `the test day`
-- FORK-01: exactly 10 years. Reading A: Blair's membership ended before the last 10 years began.
#ASSERT `the first day of the last 10 years ending on` `the test day` EQUALS `the day` 2018 6 16
#ASSERT NOT `has a disqualifying political affiliation on` `Blair` `the test day`
#ASSERT `has a disqualifying political affiliation on` `Blair's twin` `the test day`
-- FORK-01, reading B: the anniversary counts, so Blair is disqualified.
#ASSERT `has a disqualifying political affiliation, reading B, on` `Blair` `the test day`
-- 29 February: the last 10 years ending on 28 February 2036 begin on 1 March 2026.
#ASSERT `the first day of the last 10 years ending on` (`the day` 2036 2 28) EQUALS `the day` 2026 3 1
-- s 8(2)(a): Blair has been a member, other than within the last 10 years (reading A); on reading B
-- Blair is disqualified, and still has the significant affiliation too.
#ASSERT `paragraph 8(2)(a) applies to` `Blair` `on` `the test day`
#ASSERT `has a significant political affiliation on` `Blair` `the test day`
#ASSERT `has a significant political affiliation, reading B of FORK-01, on` `Blair` `the test day`
-- Casey's membership ran from 2016 to 2020, so it falls partly outside the last 10 years:
-- Casey has a disqualifying and a significant affiliation at once (ENCODING-NOTES.md, E-07).
#ASSERT `paragraph 8(2)(a) applies to` `Casey` `on` `the test day`
-- s 8(2)(b)
#ASSERT `has a significant political affiliation on` `Gray` `the test day`
#ASSERT `has a significant political affiliation, reading B of FORK-02, on` `Gray` `the test day`
#ASSERT NOT `has a significant political affiliation on` `Harper` `the test day`
#ASSERT NOT `has a significant political affiliation on` `Indy's colleague` `the test day`
#ASSERT NOT `has a significant political affiliation on` `Lee` `the test day`
#ASSERT `has a significant political affiliation on` `Lee` (`the day` 2028 7 1)
-- FORK-02: an electorate employee of a Minister (Finley) or of a shadow Minister (Indy).
#ASSERT `has a significant political affiliation on` `Finley` `the test day`
#ASSERT NOT `has a significant political affiliation, reading B of FORK-02, on` `Finley` `the test day`
#ASSERT `has a significant political affiliation on` `Indy` `the test day`
#ASSERT NOT `has a significant political affiliation, reading B of FORK-02, on` `Indy` `the test day`
-- s 8(2)(c)
#ASSERT `has a significant political affiliation on` `Kai` `the test day`
-- FORK-03: Jordan's party was not registered while Jordan held office, and is now.
#ASSERT NOT `has a significant political affiliation on` `Jordan` `the test day`
#ASSERT `has a significant political affiliation, reading B of FORK-03, on` `Jordan` `the test day`
-- s 8(2)(d)
#ASSERT NOT `has a significant political affiliation on` `Morgan` (`the day` 2028 4 30)
#ASSERT `has a significant political affiliation on` `Morgan` (`the day` 2028 5 1)
#ASSERT NOT `has a significant political affiliation on` `Alex` `the test day`
#ASSERT NOT `has a significant political affiliation on` `Ellis` `the test day`

§ `Part 3 -- ss 12 and 13`

-- Japan: one Committee, established Tuesday 11 January 2028, given its list on Tuesday 18 January
-- (7 days later), a 2-1 vote to recommend Alex, notice on Monday 20 March 2028.
`the Japan list` MEANS LIST `listed without reasons` `Alex`, `listed with reasons` `Finley`, `listed without reasons` `Ellis`
`Japan Committee` MEANS `a Committee established on` (`the day` 2028 1 11) `, given on` (`the day` 2028 1 18) `the list` `the Japan list` `, meeting with` 3 `present voting` 2 `to` 1 `, giving on` (`the day` 2028 3 20) `notice` (`recommending` "Alex")

#ASSERT `the Committee's membership complies with s 12(3) to (5)` `Japan Committee`
#ASSERT `the Committee` `Japan Committee` `is in existence on` (`the day` 2028 3 19)
#ASSERT NOT `the Committee` `Japan Committee` `is in existence on` (`the day` 2028 3 20)
#ASSERT `the Committee` `Japan Committee` `is dissolved by` (`the day` 2028 3 20)
-- s 12(8): no second Committee while the first exists; one may be established the day it dissolves.
#ASSERT NOT `section 12(8) allows a Committee to be established on` (`the day` 2028 2 1) `beside` (LIST `Japan Committee`)
#ASSERT `section 12(8) allows a Committee to be established on` (`the day` 2028 3 20) `beside` (LIST `Japan Committee`)
-- s 13
#ASSERT `the meeting was quorate` `Japan Committee`
#ASSERT `the question was carried` `Japan Committee`
#ASSERT `the decision was made at a quorate meeting` `Japan Committee`

`an inquorate Committee` MEANS `a Committee established on` (`the day` 2028 1 11) `, given on` (`the day` 2028 1 18) `the list` `the Japan list` `, meeting with` 2 `present voting` 2 `to` 0 `, giving on` (`the day` 2028 3 1) `notice` (`recommending` "Alex")
#ASSERT NOT `the meeting was quorate` `an inquorate Committee`
#ASSERT NOT `the Committee made a recommendation` `an inquorate Committee`

-- FORK-07: one vote for, none against, two abstaining.
`an abstaining Committee` MEANS `a Committee established on` (`the day` 2028 1 11) `, given on` (`the day` 2028 1 18) `the list` `the Japan list` `, meeting with` 3 `present voting` 1 `to` 0 `, giving on` (`the day` 2028 3 1) `notice` (`recommending` "Alex")
#ASSERT NOT `the question was carried` `an abstaining Committee`
#ASSERT `the question was carried, reading B` `an abstaining Committee`
#ASSERT NOT `the Committee` `an abstaining Committee` `agrees on the candidate named` "Alex"
#ASSERT `the Committee` `an abstaining Committee` `agrees, reading B of FORK-07, on the candidate named` "Alex"

§ `Part 2 -- s 10`

-- s 10(1) and FORK-05: established Tuesday 11 January; the list given Tuesday 18 January is in
-- time on reading A (last day the 7th day after, 18 January) and late on reading B (last day
-- Monday 17 January).
